{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-S-job-envelopes.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-S (campaign c2-resume, host x86-main = shared-contract owner; owner Claude Opus; worker Codex)\nGoal: the minimal shared job/handoff meaning between our Lab Manager and a lab receiver (other team's lab agent, or our clearly-labelled thin reference adapter), built FROM EXISTING records — not a new framework.\nRead: cc/engine_handoff/{README.md,engine_handoff.py} (archive observation, requirements check), cc/build_engine/README.md (build-record schema 2), bin/lab (cmd_submit spec incl. new `inputs`, cmd_run states, result.json fields, export MANIFEST), MANAGER-DESIGN.md, LAB-FEASIBILITY.md. Real records: builds/results/b0-baseline-5/build-record.json, lab/jobs/job-ad883810b3/{job.json,att-1/state.jsonl,att-1/result.json}, lab/jobs/job-8df3c7bb27 (att-1 interrupted, att-2 completed).\nDeliver in cc/engine_handoff/ (new files; edit engine_handoff.py only if you need a shared helper):\n1. `envelopes.py`: (a) `make_proposal(build_record, job_spec, host_profile, policy)` -> `campaign-job-proposal/0` dict with: campaign/request/experiment/attempt ids; target {host_id, platform, required_capabilities, platform_compat (e.g. jetpack_l4t for Jetson, cuda_arch, driver_min)}; release {role, source commit/tree, patch sha, cmake defines, transport {kind docker-archive, sha256, bytes}, image config id, index digest, executables sha256, build_record_ref}; inputs (model/prompt/test-definition hashes from spec.inputs); invocation {argv per test, mounts by ROLE with access ro/rw — no host paths}; policy {wall time, capture bytes, memory {domain, budget_bytes, guarantee: none|cooperative-intercept|cgroup-host|hard, accounting_method}, gpu_jobs_on_host:1}; evidence {controller_outside_test_sandbox, durable_destination_ref, outputs}; `unresolved` list. `dispatchable` is computed (true only if no unresolved identity). (b) `check_admission(proposal, host_profile)` -> {decision: accepted|rejected|needs-information, reasons} — rejects platform/arch mismatch (e.g. linux/amd64 sm_120 image to a jetson-arm linux/arm64 sm_87 host), missing inputs, unsupported memory guarantee; acceptance != execution. (c) `make_result(job_dir, attempt)` -> `campaign-job-result/0` with SEPARATE fields execution_outcome, test_assessment, claim_category (passed in, default 'unclassified'), evidence_completeness {expected, started, clean, missing}, last_durable_sequence (line count/last ts of state.jsonl), resource_generation (attempt + owner token sha), stop_confirmed, artifact refs (path+sha256 from MANIFEST). Never a single success boolean.\n2. `hosts/x86-main.json` (from facts: x86_64, Ryzen 7 3700X 16 threads, 46 GiB RAM, RTX 5070 Ti 16303 MiB sm_120, driver 595.99.02, CUDA 12.8 images, docker+nvidia runtime, memory guarantees available: cooperative-intercept (gpu_budget shim, D021/D023), cgroup-host) and `hosts/jetson-arm.TEMPLATE.json` with nulls + notes for the Jetson lead to fill (linux/arm64, sm_87, shared DRAM, tegrastats).\n3. CLI: `envelopes.py proposal|admit|result ...` writing JSON; pytest tests using the real records above as fixtures (copy small JSONs into cc/engine_handoff/fixtures/envelopes/), including rejection of an amd64 image on the jetson template and needs-information for a proposal without transport sha.\nAllowed writes: cc/engine_handoff/** (new files + minimal helper edits), artifacts/codexS/. 45 min, no Docker, no network. Final message: files, pytest result, field list, open questions for the lab-agent team.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
