{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat cc/engine_handoff/README.md cc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py cc/build_engine/README.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat cc/engine_handoff/README.md cc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py cc/build_engine/README.md'","aggregated_output":"# Engine handoff receipt tool\n\n`engine_handoff.py` inspects delivery bytes and requester requirements offline.\nIt never imports an image or launches a workload. Python 3 and PyYAML are\nrequired; pytest is used for tests. Optional GGUF header inspection uses the\nbundled gguf-py and its existing NumPy dependency, without loading model tensors.\nNo network or Docker is used.\n\n## Archive observations\n\n`observe_archive(path)` returns `image_config_id`, `platform`, `layer_count`, and\n`executables` (absolute `/app/...` names mapped to SHA-256). It supports classic\nDocker `manifest.json` archives and OCI `index.json`/`blobs/sha256` archives,\nincluding nested OCI indexes and Docker attestation descriptors. It admits one\nrunnable image; ambiguous multi-image deliveries are rejected.\n\nThe outer archive is indexed by member headers without extraction. Layers are\nstreamed as plain or gzip tars. Only executable regular files under `app/` are\nhashed into the merged view. Later entries override earlier entries; whiteouts\nremove lower files/subtrees, and opaque whiteouts hide lower directory contents\nwithout hiding files added in the same layer. Non-executable replacements and\nsymlinks remove previous regular-file identities. Symlinks and hardlinks are not\nfollowed or included as regular executables. Executable shared libraries count.\nMemory holds headers, paths, hashes, and bounded stream buffers, never a whole\nlayer or executable. Layer tar headers are discarded as they are consumed.\nMetadata documents have an 8 MiB limit. Archive path traversal and duplicate outer\nmembers are rejected.\n\nThe config's bytes must hash to its filename. This config digest is the image\nconfig ID; an OCI index or manifest digest is a different identity. Content-addressed\nlayer blob names are verified, and config `rootfs.diff_ids` are checked against\nthe uncompressed layer bytes when present. This detects corruption outside\n`app/` too. A classic archive without layer digests or diff_ids can still be bound\nto its recomputed outer archive hash, but lacks those additional integrity checks.\n\n## Facts, declarations, and generation\n\n```bash\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 cc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py facts \\\n  --build-record builds/results/b0-baseline-3/build-record.json \\\n  --archive builds/results/b0-baseline-3/engine-image.docker.tar \\\n  --model-config /home/muk/models/campaign/granite-3.1-1b-a400m-instruct/config.json \\\n  --gguf /home/muk/models/campaign/gguf/granite-3.1-1b-a400m-instruct-bf16.gguf \\\n  --out-dir cc/engine_handoff/example-real\n\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 cc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py generate \\\n  --facts cc/engine_handoff/example-real/facts.json \\\n  --requirements cc/engine_handoff/example/requirements.granite.yaml \\\n  --out cc/engine_handoff/example-real/handoff.yaml \\\n  --invocation-argv /app/llama-completion -m MODEL -n 24\n\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 cc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py validate \\\n  cc/engine_handoff/example-real/handoff.yaml\n```\n\n`facts` writes JSON and Markdown. Facts have a value, `observed`/`declared`/`missing`\ntag, and source. Nested Build CC schema-version-1 records are normalized, while\nall original claims remain declared. Image config ID, platform, layer count, and\nexecutable hashes are observed independently from the archive, with its path as\nsource. Archive hashes and sizes are recomputed. Identity mismatches go into\n`unresolved`. Other build metadata stays declared without being represented as\nan independently verified identity or an admission requirement.\n\n`generate` fills release identities only from archive observations. Optional\n`--requirements FILE.yaml` supplies handoff ID, release role, model references\nand manifest, workload artifact, GPU/runtime/resource/network requirements, test\nrequests, test policy, and profiling request/tool. Each copied requester value\nhas a `declared` entry in the handoff's `provenance`; archive identity provenance\nremains `observed`. The workload hash is computed from its bytes and tagged\nobserved, while its requester-provided path stays declared. No requester value\ncan override an observed release identity. Requirements workload paths resolve\nrelative to the requirements file. Other artifact references resolve relative\nto the handoff at validation; absolute manifest references are convenient.\n\n`--workload` remains supported when requirements do not supply the artifact.\nRequirements take precedence for fields they supply. Missing fields remain null\nand listed in `unresolved`. A null profiling tool is allowed when profiling is\nexplicitly false. Put options before `--invocation-argv`; everything after it is\na literal argv element. No shell expansion or execution occurs.\n\nWithout GGUF input the six unavailable header facts are listed in `unresolved`.\nHF config bytes serve as a minimal metadata manifest and do not bind model\nweights/tokenizer. Requirements and facts are provenance records, not signed\nattestations or proof of requester authority.\n\n## Validation and boundaries\n\nValidation prints a JSON receipt verdict and returns 0 for `accepted`, 2 for\n`rejected` or `needs-information`. It rehashes archive, model manifest and workload\nand re-observes every locally readable archive. It compares the handoff's config\nID, platform and full executable map directly with those observations, even if\nthe outer hash/size still match. A blob integrity failure identifies the layer\nor config and failed SHA-256 check. It also rereads the normalized build record\nand compares its identity claims. A record's incomplete executable map remains\na discrepancy, even when its listed tools match a subset of the observed map.\n\nInvalid identities, malformed/ambiguous YAML, forbidden execution keys/strings,\nshell launchers, unsupported platform, network access after staging, nonallowlisted\nmounts and policy violations are rejected. Missing readable artifacts or explicit\nunresolved entries require information unless another check rejects the receipt.\nThe allowed mounts are model:ro, workload:ro and results:rw. The lab retains\nprovisioning/isolation ownership and the external durable-evidence/crash/resume\ncontract. Acceptance is a receipt check, separate from job execution or test\nsuccess; the existing `bin/lab` remains the executor.\n\nArchive checks establish byte identity and consistency, not authenticity,\nprovenance, numerical correctness, model completeness, executable safety, GPU\navailability, runtime compatibility or actual isolation/resource enforcement.\nKeep artifacts immutable between inspection and execution; this tool does not\nhold them for a later executor.\n\n## Tests and retained real run\n\n```bash\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m pytest -q cc/engine_handoff \\\n  --basetemp=cc/engine_handoff/.test-tmp \\\n  -o cache_dir=cc/engine_handoff/.pytest_cache\n```\n\nThe original 48 checks remain, updated to expect archive-derived identities.\nThe inert 20 KiB fixture now uses `/app/run`. Additional small tarfile-built\nfixtures cover both layouts, gzip/plain layers, whiteouts and replacements,\nconfig/layer tampering, edited handoff identities with untouched transport\nhash/size, requester provenance, partial requirements and record discrepancies.\n\nThe integration evidence motivating this change is\n`experiments/handoff-real/{facts.json,handoff.yaml,verdict.json}`: generation had\nleft identities null because it treated all build-record identities as claims.\nThe T-K run is retained in `example-real/`, including facts, requirements,\nworkload, generated handoff, verdict and timings. Reproduction is available in\n`artifacts/codexK/run_real.py`; findings are in `artifacts/codexK/REPORT.md`.\nOlder captures in `example/` predate this follow-up; use `example-real/` for the\nretained real-archive observation result and `example/requirements.granite.yaml`\nfor the sample requester declaration.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Offline receipt inspection. Never imports an image or launches a workload.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport gzip\nimport posixpath\nimport tarfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport sys\n\nimport yaml\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nGGUF_PY = ROOT.parents[1] / \"ref/llama.cpp/gguf-py\"\nFORMAT = \"engine-lab-handoff-draft/0\"\nSHA = re.compile(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\\Z\")\nCLAIMS = (\"image_config_id\", \"archive_sha256\", \"archive_bytes\", \"executable_sha256\",\n          \"platform\", \"base_image_digests\", \"source_commit\", \"patch_sha256\", \"status\")\n\n\ndef digest(path):\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    size = 0\n    with Path(path).open(\"rb\") as stream:\n        for block in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n            h.update(block)\n            size += len(block)\n    return h.hexdigest(), size\n\n\ndef read_json(path):\n    with Path(path).open() as stream:\n        return json.load(stream)\n\n\ndef fact(value, tag=\"observed\", source=None):\n    return {\"value\": value, \"tag\": tag, \"source\": source}\n\n\ndef gguf_header(path):\n    \"\"\"Use the bundled gguf-py parser, stopping before ALL tensor processing.\n\n    Its read-only mmap reserves address space; only metadata pages are accessed.\n    NumPy is an existing transitive dependency of gguf-py, not of the core CLI.\n    \"\"\"\n    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(GGUF_PY))\n    from gguf import GGUFReader\n\n    class MetadataComplete(Exception):\n        pass\n\n    class HeaderReader(GGUFReader):\n        def _build_tensor_info(self, offs, count):\n            raise MetadataComplete\n\n    reader = HeaderReader.__new__(HeaderReader)\n    try:\n        try:\n            reader.__init__(str(path), mode=\"r\")\n        except MetadataComplete:\n            pass\n        arch_field = reader.get_field(\"general.architecture\")\n        arch = arch_field.contents() if arch_field else None\n        keys = {\"arch\": \"general.architecture\", \"file_type\": \"general.file_type\"}\n        keys.update({name: f\"{arch}.{name}\" for name in (\n            \"expert_count\", \"expert_used_count\", \"block_count\", \"context_length\")})\n        return {name: fact(reader.get_field(key).contents() if reader.get_field(key) else None,\n                           tag=\"observed\" if reader.get_field(key) else \"missing\",\n                           source=f\"{path}#{key}\") for name, key in keys.items()}\n    finally:\n        # Drop views before closing the mapping; no tensor arrays were constructed.\n        if hasattr(reader, \"fields\"):\n            reader.fields.clear()\n        if hasattr(reader, \"data\"):\n            reader.data._mmap.close()\n\n\ndef normalize_build_record(record):\n    \"\"\"Accept the Build CC's nested record (cc/build_engine, schema_version 1) as well as the flat claim form.\n    Adds flat claim keys derived ONLY from fields the Build CC actually recorded; flat inputs pass through unchanged.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(record, dict) or record.get(\"schema_version\") != 1:\n        return record\n    out = dict(record)\n    image, archive, tools, source = (record.get(k) or {} for k in (\"image\", \"archive\", \"tools\", \"source\"))\n    derived = {\n        \"image_config_id\": image.get(\"config_digest\") or image.get(\"Id\"),   # prefer the archive-derived config digest; Id may be an index digest\n        \"archive_sha256\": archive.get(\"sha256\"), \"archive_bytes\": archive.get(\"bytes\"),\n        \"executable_sha256\": dict(sorted((record.get(\"app_files\") or tools).items())) or None,   # all /app files when recorded\n        \"source_commit\": source.get(\"commit\"),\n        \"base_image_digests\": {k: (v or {}).get(\"reference\") for k, v in (record.get(\"base_images\") or {}).items()} or None,\n    }\n    for key, value in derived.items():\n        out.setdefault(key, value)\n    return out\n\n\nclass HashReader:\n    \"\"\"Hash a stream as it is consumed, without buffering its contents.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, stream):\n        self.stream = stream\n        self.hash = hashlib.sha256()\n\n    def read(self, size=-1):\n        data = self.stream.read(size)\n        self.hash.update(data)\n        return data\n\n    def drain(self):\n        while self.read(1024 * 1024):\n            pass\n        return self.hash.hexdigest()\n\n\ndef archive_name(name):\n    # No extraction occurs, but ambiguous traversal names must not gain identity.\n    if not isinstance(name, str) or \"..\" in name.split(\"/\"):\n        raise ValueError(f\"unsafe archive path: {name!r}\")\n    return posixpath.normpath(name.removeprefix(\"/\"))\n\n\ndef observe_archive(path):\n    \"\"\"Observe a single image without extraction; memory holds only metadata/hashes.\n\n    Outer tar members are seeked, layer tars are streamed, and both compressed\n    blob digests and uncompressed config rootfs diff_ids are checked when present.\n    Multi-image archives are rejected rather than choosing an arbitrary image.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        with tarfile.open(path, \"r:*\") as outer:\n            members = {}\n            for member in outer:\n                name = archive_name(member.name)\n                if name in members:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"duplicate archive member: {name}\")\n                members[name] = member\n\n            def stream(name):\n                name = archive_name(name)\n                member = members.get(name)\n                if member is None or not member.isfile():\n                    raise ValueError(f\"missing regular archive member: {name}\")\n                return outer.extractfile(member)\n\n            def metadata(name, expected=None):\n                with stream(name) as src:\n                    data = src.read(8 * 1024 * 1024 + 1)\n                if len(data) > 8 * 1024 * 1024:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"archive metadata too large: {name}\")\n                actual = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()\n                named = (name.split(\"/\")[-1] if name.startswith(\"blobs/sha256/\")\n                         else posixpath.basename(name).removesuffix(\".json\"))\n                if (SHA.fullmatch(named) and actual != named) or (expected and expected != \"sha256:\" + actual):\n                    raise ValueError(f\"config/metadata SHA-256 mismatch: {name}\")\n                return json.loads(data), actual\n\n            layer_digests = {}\n            if \"manifest.json\" in members:\n                manifest, _ = metadata(\"manifest.json\")\n                if not isinstance(manifest, list) or len(manifest) != 1:\n                    raise ValueError(\"archive must contain exactly one image\")\n                config_name = manifest[0][\"Config\"]\n                layers = manifest[0][\"Layers\"]\n            else:\n                index, _ = metadata(\"index.json\")\n                def images(node, depth=0):\n                    if depth > 8:\n                        raise ValueError(\"OCI index nesting too deep\")\n                    if \"manifests\" not in node:\n                        return [node]\n                    found = []\n                    for descriptor in node[\"manifests\"]:\n                        if descriptor.get(\"annotations\", {}).get(\"vnd.docker.reference.type\") == \"attestation-manifest\":\n                            continue\n                        dg = descriptor[\"digest\"]\n                        if not re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", dg):\n                            raise ValueError(\"unsupported OCI digest: \" + dg)\n                        child, _ = metadata(\"blobs/sha256/\" + dg[7:], dg)\n                        found.extend(images(child, depth + 1))\n                    return found\n                manifests = images(index)\n                if len(manifests) != 1:\n                    raise ValueError(\"OCI archive must contain exactly one runnable image\")\n                manifest = manifests[0]\n                config_name = \"blobs/sha256/\" + manifest[\"config\"][\"digest\"].removeprefix(\"sha256:\")\n                layers = []\n                for descriptor in manifest[\"layers\"]:\n                    dg = descriptor[\"digest\"]\n                    if not re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", dg):\n                        raise ValueError(\"unsupported OCI layer digest: \" + dg)\n                    name = \"blobs/sha256/\" + dg[7:]\n                    layers.append(name)\n                    layer_digests[name] = dg[7:]\n            config, config_sha = metadata(config_name)\n            named = posixpath.basename(config_name).removesuffix(\".json\")\n            if not SHA.fullmatch(named):\n                raise ValueError(\"config blob name must be its SHA-256: \" + config_name)\n            diff_ids = config.get(\"rootfs\", {}).get(\"diff_ids\")\n            if diff_ids is not None and len(diff_ids) != len(layers):\n                raise ValueError(\"config rootfs.diff_ids count differs from layer count\")\n            executables = {}\n            for i, name in enumerate(layers):\n                changes, removals, directory_replacements = {}, [], set()\n                with stream(name) as src:\n                    raw = HashReader(src)\n                    # BufferedReader needs a richer IO interface; use the seekable\n                    # outer member only to sniff the gzip magic before streaming.\n                    magic = src.read(2)\n                    src.seek(0)\n                    decoded = gzip.GzipFile(fileobj=raw) if magic == b\"\\x1f\\x8b\" else raw\n                    unpacked = HashReader(decoded)\n                    with tarfile.open(fileobj=unpacked, mode=\"r|\") as layer:\n                        for entry in layer:\n                            p = archive_name(entry.name)\n                            parent, leaf = posixpath.split(p)\n                            if leaf == \".wh..wh..opq\":\n                                removals.append(parent + \"/\" if parent else \"\")\n                            elif leaf.startswith(\".wh.\"):\n                                removals.append(posixpath.join(parent, leaf[4:]))\n                            elif p == \"app\" or p.startswith(\"app/\"):\n                                if entry.isdir():\n                                    directory_replacements.add(\"/\" + p)\n                                    changes.pop(\"/\" + p, None)\n                                else:\n                                    removals.append(p)\n                                    for key in list(changes):\n                                        if key == \"/\" + p or key.startswith(\"/\" + p + \"/\"):\n                                            del changes[key]\n                                    if entry.isfile():   # every regular file under app/ (binaries AND libraries), matching the Build CC policy\n                                        h = HashReader(layer.extractfile(entry))\n                                        changes[\"/\" + p] = h.drain()\n                            # TarFile otherwise retains every layer header.\n                            layer.members.clear()\n                    diff_sha = unpacked.drain()\n                    blob_sha = raw.drain()\n                    if magic == b\"\\x1f\\x8b\":\n                        decoded.close()\n                expected = layer_digests.get(name)\n                if name.startswith(\"blobs/sha256/\"):\n                    expected = name.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[1]\n                if expected and blob_sha != expected:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"layer blob SHA-256 mismatch: {name}\")\n                if diff_ids is not None and diff_ids[i] != \"sha256:\" + diff_sha:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"layer uncompressed SHA-256 mismatch (rootfs.diff_ids[{i}]): {name}\")\n                # Whiteouts affect the lower view regardless of order in the tar.\n                for p in removals:\n                    target = \"/\" + p\n                    for key in list(executables):\n                        if key == target or key.startswith(target.rstrip(\"/\") + \"/\"):\n                            del executables[key]\n                for key in directory_replacements:\n                    executables.pop(key, None)\n                executables.update(changes)\n            return {\"image_config_id\": \"sha256:\" + config_sha,\n                    \"platform\": f\"{config['os']}/{config['architecture']}\",\n                    \"layer_count\": len(layers), \"executables\": dict(sorted(executables.items()))}\n    except (tarfile.TarError, OSError, EOFError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError) as exc:\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid image archive: {exc}\") from exc\n\n\ndef collect_facts(record_path, archive_path, config_path, gguf=None):\n    record_path, archive_path, config_path = [Path(p).resolve() for p in\n                                             (record_path, archive_path, config_path)]\n    record, config = normalize_build_record(read_json(record_path)), read_json(config_path)\n    if not isinstance(record, dict) or not isinstance(config, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"build record and HF config must be JSON objects\")\n    archive_sha, archive_bytes = digest(archive_path)\n    config_sha, _ = digest(config_path)\n    record_sha, _ = digest(record_path)\n    result = {\n        \"format\": \"engine-lab-facts/0\",\n        \"archive\": {\"artifact\": fact(str(archive_path)), \"sha256\": fact(archive_sha),\n                    \"bytes\": fact(archive_bytes)},\n        \"build_record\": {\"artifact\": fact(str(record_path)), \"sha256\": fact(record_sha),\n                         \"claims\": {k: fact(v, \"declared\", str(record_path))\n                                    for k, v in record.items()}},\n        \"model_config\": {\"artifact\": fact(str(config_path)), \"sha256\": fact(config_sha),\n                         \"values\": {k: fact(v, source=str(config_path)) for k, v in config.items()}},\n        \"gguf\": {}, \"unresolved\": [],\n    }\n    try:\n        observation = observe_archive(archive_path)\n        result[\"archive\"].update({k: fact(v, source=str(archive_path)) for k, v in observation.items()})\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        result[\"unresolved\"].append(f\"archive observation failed: {exc}\")\n    for name in CLAIMS:\n        result[\"build_record\"][\"claims\"].setdefault(name, fact(None, \"missing\", source=str(record_path)))\n    if gguf:\n        result[\"gguf\"] = gguf_header(Path(gguf).resolve())\n    else:\n        result[\"gguf\"] = {k: fact(None, \"missing\") for k in (\n            \"arch\", \"expert_count\", \"expert_used_count\", \"block_count\", \"file_type\", \"context_length\")}\n    for claim, key in ((\"image_config_id\", \"image_config_id\"), (\"platform\", \"platform\"),\n                       (\"executable_sha256\", \"executables\")):\n        actual = observed(result[\"archive\"].get(key))\n        if record.get(claim) != actual:\n            result[\"unresolved\"].append(f\"build_record.{claim}: differs from observed archive\")\n    # Ancillary build metadata stays declared; it is not an admission identity.\n    for name, value in result[\"gguf\"].items():\n        if value[\"tag\"] == \"missing\":\n            result[\"unresolved\"].append(f\"gguf.{name}: missing\")\n    for key, actual in ((\"archive_sha256\", archive_sha), (\"archive_bytes\", archive_bytes)):\n        if record.get(key) != actual:\n            result[\"unresolved\"].append(f\"build_record.{key}: differs from observed archive\")\n    return result\n\n\ndef observed(node):\n    return node.get(\"value\") if isinstance(node, dict) and node.get(\"tag\") == \"observed\" else None\n\n\ndef generate(facts, workload, argv, requirements=None, requirements_source=None):\n    \"\"\"Copy archive observations and explicitly tagged requester declarations.\"\"\"\n    archive = facts[\"archive\"]\n    model = facts[\"model_config\"]\n    workload = Path(workload).resolve() if workload else None\n    workload_sha = digest(workload)[0] if workload else None\n    handoff = {\n        \"format\": FORMAT, \"status\": \"received\", \"handoff_id\": None,\n        \"release\": {\n            \"role\": None, \"platform\": observed(archive.get(\"platform\")),\n            \"transport\": {\"kind\": \"docker-archive\", \"artifact\": observed(archive[\"artifact\"]),\n                          \"sha256\": observed(archive[\"sha256\"]), \"bytes\": observed(archive[\"bytes\"])},\n            \"expected_image_config_id\": observed(archive.get(\"image_config_id\")),\n            \"build_record\": observed(facts[\"build_record\"][\"artifact\"]),\n            \"executable_sha256\": observed(archive.get(\"executables\")),\n        },\n        \"inputs\": {\"model\": {\"repository\": None, \"revision\": None,\n                             \"manifest\": observed(model[\"artifact\"]),\n                             \"manifest_sha256\": observed(model[\"sha256\"])},\n                   \"workload\": {\"artifact\": str(workload) if workload else None, \"sha256\": workload_sha}},\n        \"invocation\": {\"argv\": argv or None,\n                       \"mounts\": [{\"input\": \"model\", \"access\": \"ro\"},\n                                  {\"input\": \"workload\", \"access\": \"ro\"},\n                                  {\"role\": \"results\", \"access\": \"rw\"}]},\n        \"sandbox_requirements\": {\"os\": \"linux\", \"gpu\": {\"vendor\": None, \"count\": None},\n                                 \"required_runtime_compatibility\": None,\n                                 \"network_after_staging\": \"none\",\n                                 \"isolation_and_provisioning_owner\": \"lab-team\",\n                                 \"resource_limits\": {\"cpus\": None, \"memory\": None, \"pids\": None, \"timeout_s\": None}},\n        \"tests\": {\"requested\": None, \"policy_reference\": None,\n                  \"profiling\": {\"requested\": None, \"tool_and_version\": None}},\n        \"evidence\": {\"control_and_durable_storage_outside_test_sandbox\": \"required\", \"outputs\": [],\n                     \"crash_outcome\": \"interrupted-attempt-with-partial-coverage\",\n                     \"resume\": \"new-attempt-after-confirmed-stop\"},\n        \"unresolved\": list(facts.get(\"unresolved\", [])),\n    }\n\n    handoff[\"provenance\"] = {}\n    for key, identity in ((\"image_config_id\", \"release.expected_image_config_id\"),\n                          (\"platform\", \"release.platform\"),\n                          (\"executables\", \"release.executable_sha256\")):\n        handoff[\"provenance\"][identity] = archive.get(key, fact(None, \"missing\"))\n    allowed = (\"handoff_id\", \"release.role\", \"inputs.model.repository\", \"inputs.model.revision\",\n               \"inputs.model.manifest\", \"inputs.model.manifest_sha256\", \"inputs.workload.artifact\",\n               \"sandbox_requirements.gpu.vendor\", \"sandbox_requirements.gpu.count\",\n               \"sandbox_requirements.required_runtime_compatibility\",\n               \"sandbox_requirements.network_after_staging\",\n               \"sandbox_requirements.resource_limits.cpus\", \"sandbox_requirements.resource_limits.memory\",\n               \"sandbox_requirements.resource_limits.pids\", \"sandbox_requirements.resource_limits.timeout_s\",\n               \"tests.requested\", \"tests.policy_reference\", \"tests.profiling.requested\",\n               \"tests.profiling.tool_and_version\")\n    if requirements is not None:\n        if not isinstance(requirements, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"requirements must be a mapping\")\n        def supplied(path):\n            node = requirements\n            for key in path.split(\".\"):\n                if not isinstance(node, dict) or key not in node:\n                    return False\n                node = node[key]\n            return True\n        for path in allowed:\n            if supplied(path):\n                parent, _, key = path.rpartition(\".\")\n                target = at(handoff, parent) if parent else handoff\n                target[key] = at(requirements, path)\n                handoff[\"provenance\"][path] = fact(target[key], \"declared\", requirements_source)\n        if supplied(\"inputs.workload.artifact\") and at(requirements, \"inputs.workload.artifact\"):\n            artifact = Path(at(requirements, \"inputs.workload.artifact\"))\n            if not artifact.is_absolute() and requirements_source:\n                artifact = Path(requirements_source).resolve().parent / artifact\n            artifact = artifact.resolve()\n            workload_sha, _ = digest(artifact)\n            handoff[\"inputs\"][\"workload\"] = {\"artifact\": str(artifact), \"sha256\": workload_sha}\n    handoff[\"provenance\"][\"inputs.workload.sha256\"] = fact(\n        handoff[\"inputs\"][\"workload\"][\"sha256\"],\n        tag=\"observed\" if handoff[\"inputs\"][\"workload\"][\"sha256\"] else \"missing\",\n        source=handoff[\"inputs\"][\"workload\"][\"artifact\"])\n\n    def missing(node, prefix=\"\"):\n        if isinstance(node, dict):\n            for k, v in node.items():\n                if k not in {\"unresolved\", \"provenance\"}:\n                    missing(v, f\"{prefix}.{k}\" if prefix else k)\n        elif node is None:\n            if prefix == \"tests.profiling.tool_and_version\" and at(handoff, \"tests.profiling.requested\") is False:\n                return\n            handoff[\"unresolved\"].append(prefix + \": missing\")\n\n    missing(handoff)\n    return handoff\n\n\ndef at(node, path):\n    for name in path.split(\".\"):\n        if not isinstance(node, dict):\n            return None\n        node = node.get(name)\n    return node\n\n\ndef validate(handoff, base):\n    errors, unknown = [], []\n\n    def reject(reason):\n        errors.append(reason)\n\n    if not isinstance(handoff, dict):\n        return {\"state\": \"rejected\", \"reasons\": [\"handoff must be a mapping\"]}\n    if handoff.get(\"format\") != FORMAT:\n        reject(\"unsupported handoff format\")\n    if handoff.get(\"status\") not in {\"received\", \"accepted\", \"rejected\", \"needs-information\"}:\n        reject(\"status must be a receipt state\")\n\n    # Scan recursively, including unused extensions. Nothing here is executed.\n    def forbidden(node, path=\"handoff\", ancestors=()):\n        if isinstance(node, (dict, list)):\n            if id(node) in ancestors:\n                reject(path + \": cyclic YAML is forbidden\")\n                return\n            ancestors = ancestors + (id(node),)\n        if isinstance(node, dict):\n            for key, value in node.items():\n                normalized = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]\", \"\", str(key).lower())\n                if any(word in normalized for word in (\"script\", \"shell\", \"cmd\", \"hostpath\", \"privileged\", \"dockersocket\")):\n                    reject(f\"{path}.{key}: forbidden execution key\")\n                forbidden(value, f\"{path}.{key}\", ancestors)\n        elif isinstance(node, list):\n            for i, value in enumerate(node):\n                forbidden(value, f\"{path}[{i}]\", ancestors)\n        elif isinstance(node, str):\n            if (\"docker.sock\" in node.lower() or \"--privileged\" in node.lower()\n                    or node.lower() in {\"script\", \"shell\", \"cmd\"}):\n                reject(path + \": forbidden execution string\")\n\n    forbidden(handoff)\n    identities = (\"release.transport.sha256\", \"release.transport.bytes\",\n                  \"release.expected_image_config_id\", \"release.executable_sha256\",\n                  \"inputs.model.manifest_sha256\", \"inputs.workload.sha256\", \"invocation.argv\")\n    for path in identities:\n        if at(handoff, path) is None:\n            reject(path + \": null or missing required identity\")\n    for path in (\"release.transport.sha256\", \"inputs.model.manifest_sha256\", \"inputs.workload.sha256\"):\n        value = at(handoff, path)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not SHA.fullmatch(value):\n            reject(path + \": expected lowercase SHA-256 hex\")\n    image = at(handoff, \"release.expected_image_config_id\")\n    if not isinstance(image, str) or not re.fullmatch(r\"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}\", image):\n        reject(\"release.expected_image_config_id: expected sha256:<64 hex>\")\n    size = at(handoff, \"release.transport.bytes\")\n    if type(size) is not int or size <= 0:\n        reject(\"release.transport.bytes: expected positive integer\")\n    executables = at(handoff, \"release.executable_sha256\")\n    if (not isinstance(executables, dict) or not executables\n            or any(not isinstance(k, str) or not k or not isinstance(v, str) or not SHA.fullmatch(v)\n                   for k, v in (executables.items() if isinstance(executables, dict) else []))):\n        reject(\"release.executable_sha256: expected nonempty executable-to-SHA-256 map\")\n    argv = at(handoff, \"invocation.argv\")\n    if not isinstance(argv, list) or not argv or any(not isinstance(v, str) or \"\\0\" in v for v in argv) or not argv[0]:\n        reject(\"invocation.argv: expected nonempty argument vector\")\n    elif isinstance(executables, dict) and argv[0] not in executables:\n        reject(\"invocation.argv[0]: executable identity missing\")\n    if isinstance(argv, list):\n        for arg in argv:\n            if isinstance(arg, str) and (Path(arg).name.lower() in {\n                \"sh\", \"bash\", \"dash\", \"zsh\", \"ksh\", \"fish\", \"csh\", \"tcsh\", \"cmd\", \"cmd.exe\",\n                \"powershell\", \"pwsh\", \"shell\", \"script\"} or arg.endswith((\".sh\", \".bat\", \".cmd\", \".ps1\"))\n                    or re.search(r\"(?:^|[\\s/])(?:sh|bash|dash|zsh|cmd(?:\\.exe)?|pwsh|powershell)\\s+(?:-c|/c|-[Cc]ommand)\\b\", arg)\n                    or re.match(r\"--(?:shell|script|cmd|host-path)(?:=|$)\", arg)):\n                reject(\"invocation.argv: shell/script execution is forbidden\")\n    platform = at(handoff, \"release.platform\")\n    if platform is None:\n        unknown.append(\"release.platform: missing\")\n    elif platform != \"linux/amd64\":\n        reject(\"release.platform: only linux/amd64 is admitted\")\n    if at(handoff, \"release.transport.kind\") != \"docker-archive\":\n        reject(\"release.transport.kind must be docker-archive\")\n    mounts = at(handoff, \"invocation.mounts\")\n    if not isinstance(mounts, list):\n        reject(\"invocation.mounts must be an allowlisted list\")\n    else:\n        seen = set()\n        for mount in mounts:\n            if not isinstance(mount, dict) or set(mount) not in ({\"input\", \"access\"}, {\"role\", \"access\"}):\n                reject(\"invocation.mounts: only input/role and access are allowed\")\n                continue\n            name = mount.get(\"input\", mount.get(\"role\"))\n            access = mount.get(\"access\")\n            if (not isinstance(name, str) or not isinstance(access, str)\n                    or (name, access) not in {(\"model\", \"ro\"), (\"workload\", \"ro\"), (\"results\", \"rw\")}\n                    or (\"role\" in mount) != (name == \"results\")):\n                reject(\"invocation.mounts: mount is outside allowlist\")\n            elif name in seen:\n                reject(\"invocation.mounts: duplicate role\")\n            else:\n                seen.add(name)\n    for path, value in {\n        \"sandbox_requirements.os\": \"linux\",\n        \"sandbox_requirements.network_after_staging\": \"none\",\n        \"sandbox_requirements.isolation_and_provisioning_owner\": \"lab-team\",\n        \"evidence.control_and_durable_storage_outside_test_sandbox\": \"required\",\n        \"evidence.crash_outcome\": \"interrupted-attempt-with-partial-coverage\",\n        \"evidence.resume\": \"new-attempt-after-confirmed-stop\",\n    }.items():\n        if at(handoff, path) != value:\n            reject(path + \": must be \" + value)\n\n    def local_file(path):\n        value = at(handoff, path)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:\n            reject(path + \": missing local artifact\")\n            return None\n        target = Path(value)\n        return target if target.is_absolute() else Path(base) / target\n\n    actual_archive = None\n    for path, hash_path in ((\"release.transport.artifact\", \"release.transport.sha256\"),\n                            (\"inputs.model.manifest\", \"inputs.model.manifest_sha256\"),\n                            (\"inputs.workload.artifact\", \"inputs.workload.sha256\")):\n        target = local_file(path)\n        if target is not None:\n            try:\n                actual, nbytes = digest(target)\n                if actual != at(handoff, hash_path):\n                    reject(path + \": SHA-256 mismatch vs recomputed bytes\")\n                if path == \"release.transport.artifact\":\n                    actual_archive = (actual, nbytes)\n                    try:\n                        inspection = observe_archive(target)\n                        for key, identity in ((\"image_config_id\", \"release.expected_image_config_id\"),\n                                              (\"platform\", \"release.platform\"),\n                                              (\"executables\", \"release.executable_sha256\")):\n                            if inspection[key] != at(handoff, identity):\n                                reject(identity + \": differs from re-observed archive\")\n                    except ValueError as exc:\n                        reject(f\"release.transport.artifact: archive observation failed: {exc}\")\n                    if nbytes != size:\n                        reject(path + \": size mismatch vs recomputed bytes\")\n            except OSError as exc:\n                unknown.append(f\"{path}: cannot read artifact ({exc})\")\n    record_path = local_file(\"release.build_record\")\n    if record_path is not None:\n        try:\n            record = normalize_build_record(read_json(record_path))\n            if not isinstance(record, dict):\n                reject(\"release.build_record: expected JSON object\")\n            else:\n                if actual_archive and (record.get(\"archive_sha256\"), record.get(\"archive_bytes\")) != actual_archive:\n                    reject(\"build-record archive hash/bytes mismatch vs recomputed bytes\")\n                for name, path in ((\"image_config_id\", \"release.expected_image_config_id\"),\n                                   (\"executable_sha256\", \"release.executable_sha256\"),\n                                   (\"platform\", \"release.platform\")):\n                    if record.get(name) != at(handoff, path):\n                        reject(\"build-record claim differs from handoff: \" + name)\n        except OSError as exc:\n            unknown.append(f\"release.build_record: cannot read ({exc})\")\n        except (ValueError, UnicodeError) as exc:\n            reject(f\"release.build_record: invalid JSON ({exc})\")\n    unresolved = handoff.get(\"unresolved\")\n    if not isinstance(unresolved, list) or any(not isinstance(v, str) for v in unresolved):\n        reject(\"unresolved must be a list of strings\")\n    elif unresolved:\n        unknown.extend(unresolved)\n    return {\"state\": \"rejected\" if errors else \"needs-information\" if unknown else \"accepted\",\n            \"reasons\": list(dict.fromkeys(errors + unknown))}\n\n\ndef markdown(facts):\n    lines = [\"# Engine handoff facts\", \"\", \"Values describe bytes or claims; no execution was performed.\", \"\"]\n\n    def walk(node, prefix=\"\"):\n        if isinstance(node, dict) and \"tag\" in node and \"value\" in node:\n            lines.append(f\"- `{prefix}` [{node['tag']}]: {json.dumps(node['value'], ensure_ascii=True)}\")\n        elif isinstance(node, dict):\n            for key, value in node.items():\n                if key not in {\"format\", \"unresolved\"}:\n                    walk(value, f\"{prefix}.{key}\" if prefix else key)\n    walk(facts)\n    lines.extend([\"\", \"## Unresolved\", \"\"] + [\"- \" + v for v in facts[\"unresolved\"]])\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    subs = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n    facts = subs.add_parser(\"facts\")\n    for name in (\"build-record\", \"archive\", \"model-config\"):\n        facts.add_argument(\"--\" + name, required=True)\n    facts.add_argument(\"--gguf\")\n    facts.add_argument(\"--out-dir\", default=str(ROOT))\n    gen = subs.add_parser(\"generate\")\n    gen.add_argument(\"--facts\", required=True)\n    gen.add_argument(\"--workload\")\n    gen.add_argument(\"--requirements\")\n    gen.add_argument(\"--out\", required=True)\n    gen.add_argument(\"--invocation-argv\", nargs=argparse.REMAINDER, required=True)\n    val = subs.add_parser(\"validate\")\n    val.add_argument(\"handoff\")\n    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n    try:\n        if args.command == \"facts\":\n            result = collect_facts(args.build_record, args.archive, args.model_config, args.gguf)\n            dest = Path(args.out_dir)\n            dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            (dest / \"facts.json\").write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n            (dest / \"facts.md\").write_text(markdown(result))\n        elif args.command == \"generate\":\n            requirements = None\n            if args.requirements:\n                with Path(args.requirements).open() as stream:\n                    requirements = yaml.load(stream, Loader=UniqueLoader)\n            workload = args.workload or at(requirements, \"inputs.workload.artifact\")\n            if workload and not args.workload and args.requirements and not Path(workload).is_absolute():\n                workload = str(Path(args.requirements).resolve().parent / workload)\n            result = generate(read_json(args.facts), workload, args.invocation_argv,\n                              requirements, str(Path(args.requirements).resolve()) if args.requirements else None)\n            Path(args.out).write_text(yaml.safe_dump(result, sort_keys=False))\n        else:\n            with Path(args.handoff).open() as stream:\n                handoff = yaml.load(stream, Loader=UniqueLoader)\n            verdict = validate(handoff, Path(args.handoff).resolve().parent)\n            print(json.dumps(verdict))\n            return 0 if verdict[\"state\"] == \"accepted\" else 2\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, IndexError, ImportError, yaml.YAMLError) as exc:\n        if args.command == \"validate\":\n            print(json.dumps({\"state\": \"rejected\", \"reasons\": [f\"invalid handoff: {exc}\"]}))\n        else:\n            print(str(exc), file=sys.stderr)\n        return 2\n    return 0\n\n\nclass UniqueLoader(yaml.SafeLoader):\n    \"\"\"Reject ambiguous duplicate keys rather than accepting the last value.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef unique_mapping(loader, node):\n    loader.flatten_mapping(node)\n    result = {}\n    for key_node, value_node in node.value:\n        key = loader.construct_object(key_node, deep=True)\n        if key in result:\n            raise ValueError(f\"duplicate YAML key: {key}\")\n        result[key] = loader.construct_object(value_node, deep=True)\n    return result\n\n\nUniqueLoader.add_constructor(yaml.resolver.BaseResolver.DEFAULT_MAPPING_TAG, unique_mapping)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n# build_engine\n\nUse this capability to turn a clean, identified local llama.cpp checkout and an optional Git patch into a local, runtime-only CUDA image and an evidence directory. It targets linux/amd64 and CUDA architecture 120 (RTX 5070 Ti). Model weights are supplied separately at runtime.\n\nRequires Python 3.12+ (stdlib only), Git, Docker daemon access, and Docker Buildx/Bake. pytest is needed only for tests. No GPU is needed to compile or collect hashes. The builder installs Ubuntu build packages with apt; an actual build needs cached packages/base layers or repository/registry access. This implementation does not download source, patches, models, or web UI assets. The existing `campaign/cuda-tools:c1` image is not used as the builder because the required builder base is the digest-pinned NVIDIA devel image.\n\n## Run\n\nRun from the campaign directory. Give every attempt a new or empty output directory. For assignment T-N, keep outputs under `cc/build_engine/` or `artifacts/codexN/`. The CLI uses the Dockerfile and Bake recipe in `cc/build_engine/recipes/`; it does not modify or use the older recipes under `builds/llamacpp/`.\n\n```bash\n# Supply the real runtime image digest from trusted/local image evidence.\nexport BASE_RUNTIME='nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-runtime-ubuntu24.04@sha256:<64-hex-digest>'\npython3 cc/build_engine/build_engine.py \\\n  --source ref/llama.cpp --commit 31288c9c6 \\\n  --tag campaign/llamacpp:c1 --out cc/build_engine/results/baseline\n```\n\nThe placeholder must be replaced; it is not a working digest. If BASE_RUNTIME is unset, the CLI inspects the local runtime tag and selects its NVIDIA RepoDigest without pulling it. Missing local images or RepoDigests fail at `base_images`. BASE_DEVEL defaults to the devel digest already recorded in `artifacts/op-309e1f95c716/stdout`; override it with a full `nvidia/cuda:12.8.1-devel-ubuntu24.04@sha256:...` reference when needed. Both bases are validated and supplied as separate name and digest Dockerfile arguments. The CLI never builds from a floating base tag.\n\nTo add a patch, save a unified Git diff to a file and add `--patch path/to/change.patch`. Source HEAD must resolve to `--commit`; tracked changes and untracked files cause rejection. The source checkout remains read-only: Git optional locks are disabled, a `git archive` snapshot is extracted under the output directory, and `git apply --check` runs there before `git apply`. Git discovery stops before the enclosing campaign repository. Binary patches supported by Git are accepted. Submodules are rejected. Git archive honors committed export attributes; ignored and untracked files and `.git` are omitted. Docker ignore files in the staged snapshot are emptied to prevent omission of tracked source. Temporary staging is removed after either result. Keep the supplied patch and original commit for rebuilding; patch bytes are identified by SHA256 but are not retained as a separate output artifact.\n\nThe image contains only the seven requested tools in `/app`, their generated shared libraries and the OpenMP runtime, on top of the CUDA runtime base. It has no compiler, source checkout, or weights. Its entrypoint is cleared, so invoke tools by full path, for example `/app/llama-bench`. Release/shared CUDA compilation uses the flags in `build-record.json`; CPU-native tuning, tests, downloaded UI, and OpenSSL are disabled. `LLAMA_CURL=OFF` is passed as requested, although this checkout treats LLAMA_CURL as deprecated. Source and patch identity are recorded as image labels; binaries' built-in Git version may say `unknown` because `.git` is not staged.\n\n## Engine variants and linkage\n\nUse repeatable `--cmake-define KEY=VALUE` options. Keys must match `^[A-Z0-9_]+$`; values must be nonempty and contain only ASCII letters, digits, or `_./:+,@%=-`. Whitespace, shell metacharacters, empty values, duplicate keys (even with identical values), and all built-in keys are rejected before output creation. This also reserves the built-in compiler-launcher and executable-linker flags. Definitions are sorted by key, passed as the `CMAKE_DEFINES` build argument as space-separated `-DKEY=VALUE` words, and stored in the runtime image label `campaign.cmake.defines` in that same format. The CLI overwrites inherited `CMAKE_DEFINES` environment values.\n\n`recipes` records the SHA256 and size of each recipe file. `recipe_sha256` hashes canonical JSON (sorted keys, compact separators) containing those file identities, all built-in flags, the definitions, and extra targets. Definition values therefore change recipe identity even when recipe bytes are unchanged; reordering definitions does not.\n\nFor the GPU budget shim, build with VMM disabled at compile time. From the campaign root, with a clean source checkout at the shown commit and local base images available:\n\n```bash\npython3 cc/build_engine/build_engine.py \\\n  --source ref/llama.cpp --commit 31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37 \\\n  --tag campaign/llamacpp:no-vmm \\\n  --out artifacts/codexN/no-vmm-build \\\n  --cmake-define GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=ON \\\n  --linkage\n```\n\n`--linkage` enables a final check after saving the image and collecting provenance. It runs one additional `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh` against the built image's config ID, with a 60-second client timeout and no GPU. It discovers `/app/libggml-cuda.so` or a versioned `/app/libggml-cuda.so.*`, runs `ldd`, and selects `readelf -Ws` or, if unavailable, `nm -D`. A pass requires a dynamic `libcudart.so*` dependency and undefined imports of exactly `cudaMalloc`, `cudaFree`, and `cudaMemGetInfo` (including versioned symbols). Other CUDA API names and defined symbols do not satisfy the check. `ldd` showing `libcudart.so.12 => not found` still establishes a dynamic dependency; this check does not establish that runtime dependencies resolve on the GPU host.\n\nThe record's `linkage` object contains `status` (`not_requested`, `passed`, `failed`, or `unavailable`), the discovered library, config ID, `libcudart_dynamic`, `undefined_imports`, each tool's return code/reason, and output paths. Missing tools, a missing library, nonzero tool exits, Docker failures, timeouts, and malformed probe output are `unavailable`; unavailable measurements are JSON null rather than false. Runtime images may lack both readelf and nm: the check explicitly records this rather than installing tools or silently claiming imports are absent.\n\nA failed or unavailable requested check sets top-level `failure_stage=\"linkage\"` and exits 1, while preserving the saved archive and other evidence. `--linkage-optional` enables the same check (even without `--linkage`) but permits a failed/unavailable result with overall success and exit 0; inspect `linkage.status` in that case. With neither flag, linkage is `not_requested`.\n\nThe probe saves `linkage.raw.txt` (framed stdout), `linkage.stderr.txt` (Docker/probe stderr), `linkage.ldd.txt`, and `linkage.symbols.txt`. Tool stderr is merged into its corresponding raw tool output. On a Docker error or malformed probe, only the first two files may be available. This ELF check does not prove allocation interception, actual pool selection, or GPU execution; the orchestrator must verify `NO_VMM = 1` and allocation events under the budget shim.\n\n## Outputs and failure handling\n\n`build-record.json` uses schema version 2. Version 1 evidence remains untouched; this capability has no build-record reader. Schema 2 adds `cmake_defines`, `recipe_sha256`, and `linkage`; `cmake_flags` includes all built-in and extra definitions. It records status, failure stage/error, requested and resolved commit, Git tree ID and dirty status, patch SHA256 or null, tag/platform, recipe SHA256 and sizes, base references/digests, Docker and Buildx versions, CMake flags, Buildx metadata, image config ID/RepoDigests/Created/Architecture/Os, tool SHA256 values, saved archive SHA256/bytes, build duration and total duration. Fields remain null or empty when a failure occurs before collection. `build_wall_seconds` measures the Bake invocation, including export; `wall_seconds` covers the whole attempt.\n\nThe other files are:\n\n- `build.stdout` and `build.stderr`: full subprocess stdout/stderr, including compiler output and diagnostics on failure. Binary Git archive output is directed to staging rather than the logs.\n- `buildx-metadata.json`: Buildx metadata, when the build produces it; retained even when the build exits nonzero.\n- `engine-image.docker.tar`: `docker save` of the immutable Docker-reported image ID, collected before runtime probes. This ID may identify an OCI index in the containerd store. Its bytes and SHA256 are recorded after saving.\n\nThe CLI exits 0 only after all required evidence collection succeeds, otherwise nonzero; `--linkage-optional` permits a recorded linkage failure. Failures include source mismatch/dirty tree, unsupported submodules, malformed or inapplicable patch, unavailable Docker/base image, build/export failure, incorrect architecture, missing binaries, save failure, or malformed archive. A failure after building can leave the tagged local image and partial evidence; inspect `failure_stage` and retry in a fresh output directory. Invalid CLI arguments, an unwritable output path, or a nonempty output directory fail before a record can be created. Existing evidence is never overwritten. The CLI does not push, prune, mount the Docker socket in an image, or operate on unrelated containers. A short-lived `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh` container hashes the tools and libraries without requesting a GPU. After resolving the tag once, saving uses the immutable Docker-reported ID. Before hashing or linkage, the archive inspector follows the OCI catalog and nested indexes to the linux/amd64 image manifest and config, skipping other platforms and attestations. It verifies the SHA256 of referenced JSON blobs and requires exactly one matching config. Classic Docker archives are supported by hashing the config bytes named in `manifest.json`. Hashing and optional linkage then use this config digest as the local `sha256:...` Docker image ID; local-only `repo@digest` references are not used. Buildx `containerimage.config.digest` is optional and is cross-checked against the archive when present. Index metadata is cross-checked when the archive retains the index. Missing, ambiguous, or inconsistent archive identities fail before runtime probes. The record keeps `Id`/`docker_reported_id`, `config_digest`, `manifest_digest`, `index_digest`, `index_manifests`, and `docker_id_in_archive_index` separate; an unavailable manifest or index digest is null. `index.json` is the archive catalog and is not assumed to be the original image index.\n\nBake requests maximum provenance and saves metadata separately. This does not imply provenance survives image loading and `docker save`. The archive inspector checks `index.json` and reachable OCI manifests for actual in-toto SLSA provenance statements. A classic Docker archive without an OCI index records `retained: false`; an SBOM or an attestation annotation alone does not count. A save or inspection failure leaves provenance unconfirmed. No signature or attestation trust verification is performed.\n\n## Validation without a build\n\nThe CLI stages its recipes in `.campaign-recipe/` inside the archived source context. Bake receives digest-pinned base references, source and patch identity, extra targets, and extra definitions from the CLI. Prefer the CLI for validation and evidence collection; direct builds using the older `builds/llamacpp/` recipes do not support these variant options.\n\nFrom the campaign directory, run:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -m pytest -q \\\n  cc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py \\\n  --basetemp=cc/build_engine/.pytest-tmp \\\n  -o cache_dir=cc/build_engine/.pytest_cache\n```\n\nTests use temporary Git repositories and mocked Docker subprocesses. They cover patch rejection, successful patch isolation, successful record schema, build failure logs/metadata, dirty or mismatched source, archive/tool hashing, provenance versus SBOM, and refusing to overwrite evidence. They also cover define validation, variant recipe identity/build arguments/labels, schema 2, captured ELF linkage fixtures, shell tool selection, config-ID versus index-ID targeting, and fatal/optional linkage failures. The T-N2 regression uses the real containerd Buildx metadata fixture without config metadata, plus constructed content-addressed OCI index/manifest/config archives (with another platform and an attestation). It checks config metadata mismatches, missing or corrupt configs, ambiguous configs, and index metadata mismatches before any runtime probe. They use no network, GPU, or real engine build.\n\nThis evidence does not prove bitwise reproducibility, runtime correctness, model accuracy, GPU compatibility/performance, or the absence of vulnerabilities. Apt package versions, compiler behavior, timestamps, and upstream build scripts can vary. Base digests and input hashes identify inputs; they do not establish equivalence to an upstream image. The orchestrator must perform the real build and runtime checks. No Docker execution or network access was performed for T-N.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat MANAGER-DESIGN.md LAB-FEASIBILITY.md; cat builds/results/b0-baseline-5/build-record.json; cat lab/jobs/job-ad883810b3/job.json lab/jobs/job-ad883810b3/att-1/state.jsonl lab/jobs/job-ad883810b3/att-1/result.json; ls -R lab/jobs/job-8df3c7bb27; rg -n 'def cmd_submit|def cmd_run|MANIFEST|inputs|result.json|owner.token|owner_token' bin/lab\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat MANAGER-DESIGN.md LAB-FEASIBILITY.md; cat builds/results/b0-baseline-5/build-record.json; cat lab/jobs/job-ad883810b3/job.json lab/jobs/job-ad883810b3/att-1/state.jsonl lab/jobs/job-ad883810b3/att-1/result.json; ls -R lab/jobs/job-8df3c7bb27; rg -n 'def cmd_submit|def cmd_run|MANIFEST|inputs|result.json|owner.token|owner_token' bin/lab\"","aggregated_output":"# Lab Manager design (derived from campaign operations; living document)\nScope: deterministic coordination only (no reasoning agent). The other team owns the lab agent / sandbox provisioning; our reference adapter is a TEMPORARY Docker-container stand-in (`bin/lab`), never claimed to be their lab.\n\n## Responsibility map\n| Actor | Owns | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Builder (coding sandbox) | source edits, patches, build CC invocations | builds/results/*/build-record.json |\n| Build CC | source+patch+bases -> runtime image + archive + record (incl. failures) | W4 attempt 1 failure record |\n| Lab Manager (controller) | immutable job spec, attempts, admission, ownership token, state log, export, registration, reconcile | lab/jobs/*, LAB-FEASIBILITY.md |\n| Lab agent (other team) | accept/reject/needs-info, choose+provision sandbox | NOT exercised |\n| Test sandbox | runs ONE test container per request; disposable; no docker socket; RO model/data | job CR1-crash |\n| Evidence store | outside sandbox: stdout/stderr streamed to files, state.jsonl, export w/ MANIFEST | lab/export/* |\n\n## Demonstrated behaviors (op/job refs)\nidempotent submit + conflicting-spec rejection (job-3d376c81fb); attempts/retry-as-new (job-9252e2d8bf att-2; job-3739814377 att-2); cancel requested != confirmed (job-93d03ebe43); runner death -> orphan container found by label+token and killed (job-e91db9b081); death during export -> resume, no rescoring (D006 fix, job-5bbc09b093); late conflicting / foreign-token result rejected (cases 4a/4b); duplicate delivery during active attempt rejected rc 8 and replacement blocked until owner gone/reconciled (job-3739814377); controlled sandbox kill -> interrupted_sandbox_terminated with coverage, never pass, controller responsive (job-3739814377 att-1).\n\n## Open / not demonstrated\nAdmission/queueing (user removed lock D007: single-job-at-a-time is procedural; no capacity model), leases/heartbeats (deliberately not used: liveness = pid+start-time and labelled containers), runner timeouts, disk/capture budgets, retention/GC, remote receiver acknowledgement states (received/accepted/rejected/needs-information are specified in engine_handoff but not yet exchanged with a real lab agent), host-loss failure domain (protected domain = sandbox/process only; evidence on same host).\n\n## Additions from the memory-objective phase (D012-D015)\nDemonstrated (job/op refs): image admission by archive: wrong sha256 -> rc 10, wrong expected config id after load -> rc 12, correct -> admitted (op \"image-load b0 archive\", builds/results/b0-baseline-3); Build CC emitted a patched engine in 18 s via ccache cache mount (builds/results/rt1) vs 7-11 min clean (b0-baseline-2: 11-min build lost to a link error; recorded as failed attempt with stage + full log); per-test memory sampling (GPU peak via nvidia-smi, container cgroup memory.peak and io.stat) with own-file cold cache and container memory limits (job-6e6b2d39b8); test definitions as data (lab/tests/*.json) with per-test env, model file, docker mounts, memory limit.\nNew requirements found by failure:\n- R-A **Interface contracts between CCs must be pinned, not described.** The handoff CC (T-E) was given a flat build-record schema; the Build CC (T-D) emitted a nested one; admission refused a genuinely good delivery (experiments/handoff-real/verdict.json). Needed: a versioned build-record schema owned by one place, plus a normalizer test across both. -> Manager/CC-registry concern, not agent reasoning.\n- R-B **Observed vs declared must be enforced by the admission tool**: values from the build record are claims; image config id, platform and executable hashes must be re-observed from the archive (T-K).\n- R-C **Concurrent work contaminates measurements** even without a GPU lock: build/compile jobs (load avg up to 18/16 threads) distorted CPU-expert speeds (D015). Admission must also cover CPU/IO load or record load average and mark runs contaminated. (GPU lock was removed by the user, D007; this is the observed cost.)\n- R-D **Memory is a first-class measurement**: GPU peak + container peak + physical reads, with cold/warm declared per test; a result without a declared cache state is not comparable.\n- R-E Delegated agents (Codex x11, Opus x1, Sonnet x1, gpt-6-astra advice x1) required written assignments, write-location scoping and independent re-verification: Codex G's and H's analysis was high quality; Codex-written code passed its own tests but the integration (R-A) failed only when two outputs met.\n# Lab core feasibility (campaign c1) — what the prototype `bin/lab` demonstrated\nScope: image = container (immutable id), tests = named definitions run inside it, job = immutable submission, attempt = one execution. No UI. Evidence: lab/jobs/*/att-*/state.jsonl, result.json; ops in evidence/orchestrator.jsonl.\n\n## Demonstrated (ran against real containers + GPU)\n| # | Guarantee | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Images bound to immutable id; same name cannot silently point at a different image | `lab image add` check |\n| 2 | Idempotent submission by key; same key + different spec rejected; job.json write-protected | job-3d376c81fb dup/conflict |\n| 3 | Happy path, 3 tests (ppl2, gen_smoke, bench_pg) in one admitted attempt; ppl2 = 7.5325 matches E001 | job-3d376c81fb/att-1 |\n| 4 | Five result sections kept separate (execution / quality / performance / evidence / cleanup) | result.json |\n| 5 | Runner SIGKILL mid-test: orphan container found by label+token, killed, attempt `interrupted`, partial stdout kept, NOT scored | job-e91db9b081 |\n| 6 | Cancellation: request != confirmed; confirmed only after owned containers gone; live runner left alone by reconcile | job-93d03ebe43 state: cancel_requested -> cancel_confirmed |\n| 7 | Death during export: staged copy retained; register rejected until durable export; reconcile resumes export without rescoring | job-5bbc09b093 |\n| 8 | Registration idempotent (identical = no-op), conflicting late result rejected (rc 6), foreign/stale token rejected (rc 5), no-durable-export rejected (rc 7) | cases 4a/4b |\n| 9 | Retry = new attempt (att-2) | job-9252e2d8bf |\n| 10 | (HISTORICAL — lock removed in D007) GPU admission by flock serialised concurrent attempts (waited 3.5 s) | job C6-conc |\n\n## Problems found (these drive the interface)\n- P1 **Lock != exclusivity.** flock vanished with the dead runner while its container kept using the GPU (case 5). Admission must be tied to the *container's* lifetime / cgroup, or reconcile must precede re-admission.\n- P2 **Recovery bug (D006):** first reconcile overwrote a finished result. Recovery must be phase-aware and results write-once. This was found only because the test killed the runner *in each phase*; \"runner died\" as one test would have missed it.\n- P3 **No per-job single-active-attempt policy.** Two invocations of one job = two attempts (case 6). Needs an explicit policy (reject / queue / coalesce).\n- P4 **Measurement confound is invisible to the lab:** SM clock at launch was 2955 MHz vs 1155 MHz across attempts; the lab records it but cannot control it. Perf tests need clock/warmup policy declared in the test, not guessed.\n- P5 **First-rep warmup** in bench_pg samples (14.9k vs ~18k t/s): raw samples must be kept; averaging hides it.\n- P6 **Root-owned outputs:** container ran as root, so converted GGUF is root-owned on the host. Cleanup/export needs a uid policy.\n- P7 **Test definitions are code in the lab, not data.** Each new test (parser + assessor) required editing `bin/lab`. A test needs a declarative contract: command, input mounts, parser, assessor, whether it needs exclusive GPU.\n- P8 **Wrapper blind spot (D001)** repeated at a larger scale: process-group tracking insufficient; label+token ownership worked.\n- P9 Host-visible only: ownership by docker label can be forged by anyone who can run docker; this is \"ownership by convention + token\", not enforcement.\n\n## Not demonstrated (proposals only)\nHeartbeat/lease handling, timeouts for the *runner* (only per-test timeout), disk/capture budgets, multi-GPU, queue fairness, retention/GC of exports, remote execution, authentication.\n- NOTE (D007): GPU lock removed by user; P1 is now moot, replaced by 'no admission control: scored runs need a per-run exclusivity check'.\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"success\",\n  \"failure_stage\": null,\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-11-09T21:16:49.571198+00:00\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"path\": \"/home/muk/projects/siminfeng/campaign/ref/llama.cpp\",\n    \"requested_commit\": \"31288c9c6\",\n    \"commit\": \"31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37\",\n    \"tree\": \"158a7ade930818efdb06c5561920a8d018d404ba\",\n    \"dirty\": false,\n    \"status_porcelain\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"patch_sha256\": null,\n  \"extra_targets\": [],\n  \"tag\": \"campaign/llamacpp:b0\",\n  \"platform\": \"linux/amd64\",\n  \"cmake_flags\": [\n    \"-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\",\n    \"-DGGML_CUDA=ON\",\n    \"-DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=120\",\n    \"-DLLAMA_CURL=OFF\",\n    \"-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON\",\n    \"-DGGML_NATIVE=OFF\",\n    \"-DLLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=OFF\",\n    \"-DLLAMA_BUILD_UI=OFF\",\n    \"-DLLAMA_USE_PREBUILT_UI=OFF\",\n    \"-DLLAMA_OPENSSL=OFF\"\n  ],\n  \"recipes\": {\n    \"Dockerfile\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"45e2ed5731d944838f51a732c0a6e2bdf5b82ff438369cf080d7ffd24708e623\",\n      \"bytes\": 2036\n    },\n    \"docker-bake.hcl\": {\n      \"sha256\": \"4bca23e965e09b10a8e62cde9088f19751eef7550e6941acc850